Subject: [PATCH] tiff: honor libtiff's Windows CRT file-descriptor interface

With AVOID_WIN32_FILEIO, TIFFFdOpen expects a CRT descriptor. Passing a
Win32 HANDLE invokes the CRT invalid-parameter handler when loading TIFFs.
Duplicate the descriptor so TIFFClose does not close the caller's stream.

--- a/gdk-pixbuf/io-tiff.c
+++ b/gdk-pixbuf/io-tiff.c
@@ -351,6 +351,18 @@
         lseek (fd, 0, SEEK_SET);
 #ifndef G_OS_WIN32
         tiff = TIFFFdOpen (fd, "libpixbuf-tiff", "r");
+#elif defined(AVOID_WIN32_FILEIO)
+        /* This libtiff uses CRT descriptors, not Win32 HANDLEs. Duplicate
+         * the descriptor because TIFFClose() and our caller both close it.
+         */
+        {
+                int tiff_fd = _dup (fd);
+                if (tiff_fd >= 0) {
+                        tiff = TIFFFdOpen (tiff_fd, "libpixbuf-tiff", "r");
+                        if (tiff == NULL)
+                                _close (tiff_fd);
+                }
+        }
 #else
         /* W32 version of this function takes HANDLE.
          * What's worse, the caller will close the file,
